cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Time to Index: a freshness and staleness benchmark for web-search APIs"
message: "If you use this benchmark or its method, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Das
    given-names: Abhijit
repository-code: "https://github.com/abhid1234/time-to-index"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  Measures how long a newly published fact takes to become retrievable through
  each web-search API, and how often the API confidently returns the answer it
  replaced. Ground truth comes from sources that stamp their own publication
  time. Latency is estimated with Turnbull's nonparametric MLE for
  interval-censored data; an origin control arm separates provider indexing
  lag from the document's own availability on the web.
keywords:
  - information retrieval
  - search
  - benchmark
  - freshness
  - survival analysis
  - interval censoring
